{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the Amalekite and the Canaanite.</b> He is the Amorite, for every Amorite is a Canaanite, and Scripture did not trouble to separate him out on account of the Amalekite, who is of the descendants of Shem, and Canaan, who is the father of the Amorite, of the descendants of Ham. So too \"the Amalekite and the Canaanite came down\" (Numbers 14:45) — and elsewhere \"the Amorite came out,\" and he did not mention the Amalekite, because the Amorite is the principal one." "<b>Dwelling in the valley.</b> To lie in ambush for you. Some say: even though the Amalekite and the Canaanite dwell in the valley, turn toward the way of the Sea of Reeds and do not fear. Now Israel did not repent; therefore HaShem spoke."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:42.373763595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}